      <aside class="rounded-lg border-l-4 border-amber-400 bg-amber-50 p-5 mb-6">
        <p class="text-xs font-sans uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-800 mb-2">
          Excluded classes — active engine work
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 leading-relaxed mb-3 max-w-3xl">
          Out of 940 post-electron-parity Burcat candidates, 290 were
          discarded by parsable structural rules (no per-molecule
          cherry-picking). Exclusion is <strong>declarative</strong>:
          these are classes for which PTC modelling is explicitly
          <em> under construction</em>. Testing PTC there today would
          produce numbers that reflect the <em>absence of a dedicated
          model</em>, not a PT prediction.
        </p>
        <details class="text-sm">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-amber-900 hover:text-amber-700">
            List of 11 excluded classes + reason →
          </summary>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 leading-relaxed pl-4">
            <li><strong>Inorganic alkali / alk-earth salts</strong> with no carbon (Li, Na, K, Cs, Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba) — pure ionic modelling not finalized.</li>
            <li><strong>Hypervalent halogenated</strong> (≥5 halogens on a central atom, e.g. ClF₅, BrF₅, IF₇) — PT hypervalent face not implemented yet.</li>
            <li><strong>p-block homonuclear clusters</strong> Xₙ with n ≥ 3 (P₄, S₃ to S₈, As₄, N₄, Sb₄) — symmetric multiple-bond clusters not covered.</li>
            <li><strong>Small ionic oxides without C/H</strong> (≤4 heavy atoms + O) — including W₃O₉ and polynuclear d-block oxide clusters.</li>
            <li><strong>Heavy main-group organometallics</strong> (Hg, Pb, Sn, Tl, Bi bonded to C).</li>
            <li><strong>Single atoms</strong> (n_atoms = 1) — atomization energy undefined.</li>
            <li><strong>Noble-gas dimers</strong> (Ar₂, Ne₂…) — van der Waals, out of engine scope.</li>
            <li><strong>Simple TM halides/sulfides</strong> (HgCl₂, ZnS, FeS, BBr…).</li>
            <li><strong>TM oxyhalides and hydroxides</strong> (WO₂Cl₂, Cr(OH)₆…).</li>
            <li><strong>p-block oxide clusters</strong> (P₄O₆, P₄O₁₀, As₄O₆…).</li>
            <li><strong>Exotic cyclic isomers of small molecules</strong> (cyclic CO₂, CH₂O₂ dioxirane…) — Burcat catalogues high-energy isomers, the PTC solver picks the global minimum.</li>
          </ul>
